flowchart TB
  accTitle: Notifications trigger trusted processing and REST supports recovery
  accDescr: Instance activity feeds the configured ZeroMQ publisher, whose stream does not apply per-user distribution filtering. A trusted consumer receives live notifications and can also query current state or reconcile through an API account with its own permissions. The consumer applies idempotent target changes. ZeroMQ is not a durable replay queue, and narrower REST permissions do not narrow data already received from the stream.
  A["MISP instance activity<br/>Includes configured private/draft activity"] --> Z["ZeroMQ live notifications<br/>Instance-wide trust boundary"]
  Z -->|"Trigger"| C["Trusted consumer queue"]
  R["REST queries and reconciliation<br/>API account's visibility"] -->|"Current authorised state"| C
  C --> T["Apply target changes by UUID<br/>Handle retries and removals"]
  classDef stream fill:#fff4df,stroke:#91651c,color:#573d13;
  classDef stage fill:#e7f6fa,stroke:#007b96,color:#153448,stroke-width:2px;
  class A,Z stream;
  class R,C,T stage;
